# already-tried-flashnext.txt - what was already tried on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on this PC, kept as data so the Qwen4 pack reuses it.
# One idea per line:  STATUS | idea | measured result | source[; source ...]
# STATUS: ADOPTED (in the served config), REJECTED (measured, dropped), PARKED (measured or built, waiting),
#         NOT MEASURED, DESK ONLY (estimate or reading only), INFO (a measured fact, not a switch).
# Sources: repo-relative path[:line or :a-b] (repo = strata-compare), notes/<note>.md[:line] (the project's notes),
#          ../<sibling folder>/<path>[:line]. profile_pack.py checks every file exists and every line is inside it.
# Text rules (the pack goes to outside readers): no names of people, no home paths, no other tools of the owner
# ("agent-workload screen" = the owner's research-agent replay screen).
# Terms: P028x = the served build; "screen" = the 9-workload speed screen (geometric mean tok/s); "fixtures" = the
# cold pp16k / pp64k prompts and the conv / struct / prose decode texts; B = the Basalt-port branch's own base build.
# Older rounds ran on older Strata releases (round 9-14 = v0.1.32-v0.1.40, 10-01..10-06); dates are 2026.
# Curated 11-09 from results/BACKLOG-1027.md, NOTES.md, HANDOFF.md, the result folders and the project notes
# (a read-only helper collected the lines; each cited line was spot-checked).

